// The KR and Enhanced terrain materials whose texture repetition KR-like, Enhanced and UOD-Painterly may break up,
// when the style's land_texture_variation is on (the land shader settings' "Break up terrain texture repetition").
// The land shader then draws each listed material's two colour layers through a grid of overlapping hexagons two
// cells wide, each hexagon showing the texture moved by its own random offset, and its blend mask through a larger
// grid of its own; materials not listed keep their plain tiling. Classic draws no materials. Dynamapper reads your
// copy, cache/runtime_specs/land/LandTextureVariation.kdl beside the assets folder, in place of this file when it
// exists, at startup: copy this file there and edit the copy. A copy that does not read leaves this file in force,
// with a warning naming the line, until it is fixed.
//
//   material <id> [<last id>] rotate=true|false
//     The material id of the KR and Enhanced terrain (tex_land_kr.uddp and tex_land_ec.uddp number them alike), or
//     every id from <id> to <last id>, 0 to 255. rotate=true also turns each hexagon by a random quarter turn: only
//     for textures with no direction and no light baked in. A material is listed once.
//
// Never list masonry, planks, tiles or furrows, whose courses must line up across the cells, nor cliffs and
// embankments, whose strata follow the slope. The seed list was checked on the colour layers and masks of every
// material, tiled 2x2, and on captures of the plains in both packages.

// Grass, dirt, forest litter and snow: no direction (snow's bump layer turns with it).
material 1 2 rotate=true
material 4 rotate=true
material 8 rotate=true
// Jungle: the detail layer has diagonal streaks.
material 3 rotate=false
// Rock and dark rock: relief lit from one side.
material 6 rotate=false
material 146 rotate=false
// Sand: dimples and ripples lit from one side.
material 7 rotate=false
// Swamp and its edges: leaves and vines.
material 48 rotate=true
material 69 rotate=true
material 129 144 rotate=true
// Dirt with large rocks: the rocks are lit from one side.
material 155 rotate=false
// Cool lava and the void destruction: an organic crust, its cracks embossed by a light from the top left.
material 193 194 rotate=false
